{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI write from Metz, the evening air cool after a long day. The town is quiet, save for the garrison officers who crowded the theatre tonight. I watched a vaudeville and a play, but my mind wandered to the view from the ramparts. The Moselle winds through the valley, a ribbon of silver in the twilight. It is a beautiful sight, reminding me of the Rhine, yet distinct in its character.\n\nI have secured a front coupé for the diligence to Paris tomorrow. The journey should be swift. I walked the streets before dinner, noting the architecture and the life within. It is good to be moving again, to see the world unfold before me. The cathedral looms large, a testament to centuries of faith and stone.\n\nI think of you and the boys in Berlin. The distance feels less when one is traveling with purpose. Pray for a smooth crossing of the frontier.\n\nYour loving,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080501,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":205,"prompt_tokens":945,"total_tokens":1150,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-Zf5IQhEmSEDPuuswNKsmPStO2lqRB0lE","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":945,"prompt_ms":950.343,"prompt_per_token_ms":1.0056539682539682,"prompt_per_second":994.3778193767935,"predicted_n":205,"predicted_ms":4835.803,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.704916666666666,"predicted_per_second":42.18534129698832}}